itle=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What about Orphan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could fit too, because I believe in the Shadowrun aspect that all magic is equal, it depend only on what you belief is working for you. So it could work with everything except technocratic principles because I can not overcome the, using magic without beliefing that it is magic or other supernatural power. There my mind would make only sense with Syndicate where there magic is being a supreme leader and bring your subordinates with your words to do what you want because they want to achieve for this shining person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T16:11:51-07:00","id":1413455,"title":"","content":"I'd have to say Orphan, just because nothing else is a close fit. Maybe a Chorister, but I'd be <i>very</i> Latitudinarian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T17:18:26-07:00","id":1413462,"title":"","content":"I'd be an ITX or Progenitor. I already work for the man IRL, it wouldn't be much of a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T06:39:24-07:00","id":1413554,"title":"","content":"Oh I\u2019m tied between Etherite or Dreamspeaker, with Akashayana right behind. Ultimately probably Dreamspeaker, I like the idea of their balance with spirits of nature or even ancestors, and the universality of their membership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T17:55:01-07:00","id":1413669,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> what makes you prefer Dreamspeakers to Verbenae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T18:34:21-07:00","id":1413679,"title":"","content":"Purely the spirit connections, spirit speaks to me more then life, and spirits as a subject of study and the subject of a magical career over sacrifice and the old ways to shapeshift or conjure storms. There was an interesting Dreamspeaker in the Ascension Novel, he had some sort of magical flaw, so it was difficult for him to learn anything past sensing magic so he developed learning the first dot of every sphere, very interesting concept I could see doing that if magic is difficult. :P Or train as an Akashic to gain serenity and balance two dots in Mind, Life and Spirit for the harmony and simplistic magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T19:32:20-07:00","id":1413688,"title":"","content":"I think I'd fit in best with Iteration X. Transcending humanity's limits with technology, forming symbiotic relations with machines and intelligence, simulations where anything becomes possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T19:53:08-07:00","id":1413691,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy, probably the New World Order. Always pick the winning side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T04:34:11-07:00","id":1413751,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> Cool. Sacrifice is important when learning magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T04:35:13-07:00","id":1413752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1413691#post1413691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy, probably the New World Order. Always pick the winning side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like your sig lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T09:25:53-07:00","id":1414748,"title":"","content":"What best suits me is to be an Orphan or multi-Tradition mage with a paradigm that combines aspects of the Order of Hermes, Verbena, Akashayana, and Sahajiva. I am surey going to stick with the Traditions but I am challenged to pick only one among these four options. The other Traditions' paradigms have little appeal for me for various reasons. I have nothing but scorn for the lowest-common-determinator authoritarianism of the Technocracy, and little respect for the narrow-minded perspective of the Disparates. The boundless solipsistic freedom and resistance to Paradox of the Marauders registers as a very serious temptation to me, but on the other hand I fear the self-inflicted limitations and lack of clarity of Quiet. The nihilism of the Nephandi feels petty and incomprehensible.<br /> <br /> More precisely, my preferred Paradigm is a combination of Creation is Divine and Alive; Everything is an Illusion; Might is Right; Transcend Your Limits; We\u2019re All God(s) in Disguise. Preferred Practices include Animalism, Bardism, Chaos Magick, Crazy Wisdom, Elementalism, Invigoration, Martial Arts, Psionics, and Yoga. Preferred Instruments are bodywork; dance, gestures, and movement; energy; eye contact; language, music, and voice; meditation; ordeals and exertions; sex and sensuality; symbols; social domination; thought forms; True Names; weapons; writing and inscriptions.To a lesser degree, also blessings and curses; cards and dice; elements: math and numerology; prayer and invocations: wands.<br /> <br /> No matter how much Satyr Phil can wax poetic with tracts about the unspeakable evil and danger of sociopathy, personal experience tells me that high-functioning sociopaths exist that can put their personality to constructive ends and not be Nephandi in training, abusers (by a non-woke definition, anyway), or a threat to anyone but their enemies. Therefore, mine is a benevolent or at least enlightened Left-Hand path as befitting my nature.<br /> <br /> A key feature of my mage self-insert is paradigm goes out of its way to minimize dependence on physical tools and ritual, and emphasize reliance on non-physical foci that can be easily used in the field. Any physical foci that get used have a secondary role and are easily carried and replaced. That's because my playstyle preferences for wizards mandate magic to be done with the mage's body and mind only or nearly so, and be fully accessible in combat or equivalent situations. Magic that needs tools or ritual for any but the most outlandish and overwhelming effects is not real magic, just a pathetic travesty of mundane tech. As you may guess, I do not get along with technomancer or ritualistic paradigms (I do love the OoH, but this element gets excised from my version of their paradigm. Less circles, more Enochian), and it is one more reason why I cannot play a technocrat at gunpoint. This playstyle preference obviously becomes a core paradigm feature in a self-insert of mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-22-2020, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T13:29:48-07:00","id":1414793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414748#post1414748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closest thing that suits me is to be an Orphan or multi-Tradition mage with a paradigm that combines aspects of the Order of Hermes, Verbena, Akashayana, and Sahajiva. The other Traditions' paradigms have little appeal for me for various reasons. I have nothing but scorn for the lowest-common-determinator authoritarianism of the Technocracy, and little respect for the narrow-minded perspective of the Disparates. The boundless solipsistic freedom of the Marauders registers as a very serious temptation to me, but on the other hand I fear the self-inflicted limitations and lack of clarity of Quiet. The nihilism of the Nephandi feels petty and incomprehensible.<br /> <br /> More precisely, preferred Paradigm is a combination of Creation is Divine and Alive; Everything is an Illusion; Might is Right; Transcend Your Limits; We\u2019re All God(s) in Disguise. Preferred Practices include Animalism, Bardism, Chaos Magick, Crazy Wisdom, Elementalism, Invigoration, Martial Arts, Psionics, and Yoga. Preferred Instruments are bodywork; dance, gestures, and movement; energy; eye contact; language, music, and voice; meditation; ordeals and exertions; sex and sensuality; symbols; social domination; thought forms; True Names; weapons; writing and inscriptions.To a lesser degree, also blessings and curses; cards and dice; elements: math and numerology; prayer and invocations: wands.<br /> <br /> No matter how much Satyr Phil can wax poetic with tracts about the unspeakable evil and danger of sociopathy, personal experience tells me that high-functioning sociopaths exist that can put their personality to constructive ends and not be Nephandi in training, abusers (by a non-woke definition, anyway), or a threat to anyone but their enemies. Therefore, mine is a benevolent or at least enlightened Left-Hand path as befitting my nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn\u2019t benevolent Left-Hand path an oxymoron?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T14:22:17-07:00","id":1414814,"title":"","content":"Akashic Brotherhood for their martial arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T14:52:35-07:00","id":1414820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414814#post1414814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Akashic Brotherhood for their martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Do you like their philosophy as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T15:39:16-07:00","id":1414830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414793#post1414793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn\u2019t benevolent Left-Hand path an oxymoron?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. Speaking from personal experience and the way I play my self-insert characters here, but selfish and amoral people with sociopathic traits can still end up doing good and acting heroically all the time for reasons different from their non-existent altruism, morality, and empathy, esp. if they are not shortsighted and have good self-control and self-awareness. Perhaps the outcome directly or indirectly benefits them in the long term or they find it pleasant or it fulfills some ideal of theirs. I do little acts of kindness this way. My OP self-inserts save the world on a regular basis and proactively strive to improve it for these reasons. E.g. &quot;People, especially [insert appropriate derogatory label for ordinary people], register as walking, talking animals or objects that matter nothing to me, at best I can care for them like pets or prized possessions. I can destroy, exploit, or manipulate them with no hesitation or remorse if it is convenient enough. Yet they make good company, create amazing culture, and are good sexual and gaming partners. I need to protect them for this. The happier they are, the better they get at the things I like them. Therefore, I have to turn the world into an utopia&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-20-2020, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T19:27:17-07:00","id":1414863,"title":"","content":"Probably an Orphan. Maybe a Son of Ether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T05:04:10-07:00","id":1414898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414830#post1414830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends. Speaking from personal experience and the way I play my self-insert characters here, but selfish and amoral people with sociopathic traits can still end up doing good and acting heroically all the time for reasons different from their non-existent altruism, morality, and empathy, esp. if they are not shortsighted and have good self-control and self-awareness. Perhaps the outcome directly or indirectly benefits them in the long term or they find it pleasant or it fulfills some ideal of theirs. I do little acts of kindness this way. My OP self-inserts save the world on a regular basis and proactively strive to improve it for these reasons. E.g. &amp;quot;People, especially [insert appropriate derogatory label for ordinary people], register as walking, talking animals or objects that matter nothing to me, at best I can care for them like pets or prized possessions. I can destroy, exploit, or manipulate them with no hesitation or remorse if it is convenient enough. Yet they make good company, create amazing culture, and are good sexual and gaming partners. I need to protect them for this. The happier they are, the better they get at the things I like them. Therefore, I have to turn the world into an utopia&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting but scary. At least your characters are honest about their worldview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T05:04:44-07:00","id":1414899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414863#post1414863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably an Orphan. Maybe a Son of Ether.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not a Hollow One?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T06:48:19-07:00","id":1414910,"title":"","content":"I'm not really a Goth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T09:01:12-07:00","id":1414926,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a> got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T09:54:02-07:00","id":1414933,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qE0UimODxNg\" target=\"_blank\">Iteration X all the way, with a splash of Progenitors.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T13:59:27-07:00","id":1414964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414898#post1414898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting but scary. At least your characters are honest about their worldview.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a fact that high-functioning sociopaths have to act a certain degree of empathy and morality all the time that they are unable to feel, understand, or respect in order to get along in society. It can be done without excessive difficulty up to a decent degree but not so rarely the burden of wearing a lifelong mask feels as tiresome and suffocating as it is necessary. I suppose the experience is not so different from the one of being a spy, a supernatural under a Masquerade, a super with a secret identity, or a LGBT person in a closet. The Dexter TV show kind of depicts how it feels even if it unfortunately endorses the Hollywood toxic stereotype that all or most persons with a psychopathic personality are (would-be) serial killers.<br /> <br /> Amassing political, social, and economic power is not for everyone and at best is a partial escape from the need to feign since even members of the elite in modern society ultimately need the goodwill of society to thrive. Misbehave enough, and you'll lose your assets and even your freedom. In our peaceful and enlightened age, the social niches where you can drop the mask and let your inner asshole surface are few and far between, such as being a professional criminal, a warlord or mercenary, and the like. If anything, it seems society is headed to narrow them even further, and the roles where sociopathic traits are adaptive (e.g. being a warrior or hunter) have shrunk. By the way, this is one reason why I am a sworn enemy of woke ideology and cancel culture. Its victory threatens the likes of me with the existential nightmare of deplatforming, ostracism, bullying, celibacy, unemployment, and poverty as the penalty for not performing an IMP extreme level of empathy for strangers that I am unable and unwilling to feel or act. Posing as the normal nice guy all the time is hard enough.<br /> <br /> Superpowers, however, would truly change the picture. Get a sufficient degree of them to be independent from society and able to fight off anything it can throw at you, and you can really drop the mask and let loose your inner jerk and murderhobo without any real consequence. Being able to RP that kind of experience is one of the aspects of gaming I find most fulfilling and liberating, and why I get incredibly upset if the possibility of playing evil characters gets restricted or punished too much. That's one reason why I generally find natural and congenial to play selfish and amoral OP characters, and why I usually find the moral paragon or underdog kind of character too alien and frustrating to play. On the other hand, my enlightened-selfishness and idealist side is also important enough that it carries through in gaming. Therefore, rather then the malevolent kind of villain, I often find preferable to play the sociopathic but noble and/or well-intentioned anti-hero or villain that ends up acting heroically, being the savior, and/or making the world a better place for reasons completely different from altruism, morality, or empathy. Of course, if the character is supposed to be a self-insert, this line of reasoning gets magnified to the Nth degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-22-2020, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T15:01:55-07:00","id":1414971,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I\u2019m an empath, the opposite. But I\u2019ve dated one or two sociopaths and your insights are appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T15:45:56-07:00","id":1414977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414971#post1414971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I\u2019m an empath, the opposite. But I\u2019ve dated one or two sociopaths and your insights are appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to be of service. ;-) Coming back to our original topic, the Left-Hand Path IMO seems about how and why you do magic. It focuses your paradigm through a lens of individualism, selfishness, rebellion, and sensation. It says relatively little about what you use magic for, although chances are you will also use it for personal gain, pleasure, and/or violence. This is far from being the whole picture, and a lot depends on your interests, goals, ideals, and the rest of your paradigm. Even more so because mages are unlikely to be the kind of shortsighted people that get superpowers and only use them to rob banks or get one-night-stands.<br /> <br /> Of course, even idealism can be easily twisted into something dark and terrible (hello, organized religion and 20th century) and one person's hero is another person's monster. E.g. my lusty &amp; transhumanist LHP character may fight the Ascension War also to make cheap and flawless fertility control spells available to everyone, b/c reproductive control usually means sexual liberation. They would also add like a ton of other personal enhancement static magic to the agenda, but you get the picture. The Nephandus next door...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-21-2020, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T17:29:44-07:00","id":1414994,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The Nephandus next door.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that\u2019s an interesting take on Left Hand Paths. I never really thought of it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T17:30:53-07:00","id":1414995,"title":"","content":"Edit: merged with other post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-22-2020, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T17:56:40-07:00","id":1414996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1414994#post1414994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. The Nephandus next door.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that\u2019s an interesting take on Left Hand Paths. I never really thought of it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am glad to share insights I harbored my entire geek life to some degree. My vision obviously evolved over time, and self-awareness about my nature occurred at a later age, but I remember myself in grade school as a precocious little nerd reading comic-books and thinking Superman sucked for being a boyscout slave to the status quo, and Dr. Doom was the real hero for wishing to conquer the world and build a technomagical utopia. Even back then, I had my role models broadly defined about what to do with superpowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-21-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T18:24:33-07:00","id":1414998,"title":"","content":"Awesome. I saw the old Lands of Dr. Doom boxed set for the Marvel Super Heroes RPG in a game store once. <br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for sharing your insights. Have a nice evening. Blessed be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T22:43:25-07:00","id":1418148,"title":"","content":"Verbena. Save the planet. Live forever.<br /> <br /> Marry a sorceress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 11-04-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T04:04:20-07:00","id":1418170,"title":"","content":"I would probably be an Orphan with some technomystical allegiances. Hell, I would probably the the kind of mage who is somehow using Pillars and Foundation still. <br /> I'd probably only get along with individual Crafts and at most Virtual Adepts, the Sons of Ether, and Technocracy members who would keep our contact on the down low. <br /> I would not partake in either side of the Ascension War, I would prefer to only pursue my own personal interests, ideals, and goals, and at most take on some acolytes who I believe would work well with me. I help people because I want to, and don't when I don't. <br /> If anyone tried to force me to pick a side, I would just play the part until I could get payback for being forced into the situation. I don't like being forced to do things if I don't choose to, and I really hate being forced into moral/ideal debates. I have my opinions/morals/ideals and I'm not changing them any time soon.<br /> Plus, I'm the kind of person who likes to remain outside of factions. I don't like being expected to follow the party line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T10:26:25-07:00","id":1418210,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think I should last a week as a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T11:54:52-07:00","id":1418221,"title":"","content":"Based on characters I've played in the past over multiple systems, and personal philosophies, I'd be, with out a doubt, Verbena. All Nature, all the time, both physical and spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 10-14-2020, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T08:25:47-08:00","id":1421800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1412992#post1412992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m sorry. The Celestial Chorus is not my religion, but it can be very inspiring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not religious and definitely not Christian or anything like that, but the CC's whole thing about everyone being a shard of the whole spirit is kinda beautiful. Also I think I might be more likely to be religious/spiritual if I had actual magic.<br /> <br /> Verbena would be my first choice though, as I dig that witchy vibe and I love me some shapeshifting skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T09:15:04-08:00","id":1421806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1421800#post1421800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not religious and definitely not Christian or anything like that, but the CC's whole thing about everyone being a shard of the whole spirit is kinda beautiful. Also I think I might be more likely to be religious/spiritual if I had actual magic.<br /> <br /> Verbena would be my first choice though, as I dig that witchy vibe and I love me some shapeshifting skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you about the Verbena and about the CC being beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T13:43:34-08:00","id":1421843,"title":"","content":"I think I've said this before on one of these threads, but NWO. I find something weirdly fascinating about their original convention book; possibly the extent to which that book just lifted from 1984.<br /> <br /> By no means claim that that's a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T14:23:21-08:00","id":1421847,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say for sure, but I would likely be a Hollow One or an Orphan who practices Chaos Magick; Everything is Chaos, with some Gods and Monsters. Perhaps a Techgnosi? What I like about Chaos Magick is that it's a mystical Paradigm that nonetheless focuses on tapping into or harnessing powers around or within us in a way that anyone can practice if they are willing to make the time and the effort, and without making any further assumptions about the One Truth of Everything.<br /> <br /> There are some Traditions that I do like; I might fit in decently with the Sahajiya/CoE in particular. But all of the Traditions involve a relatively strong commitment to some kind of fundamental Truth or Teleology that I'm just not willing to buy into 100%. Similarly, one thing I do like about the more idealistic side of the Technocracy/OoR, and idea that getting into MtA really brought to my attention, is the notion that the benefits of science/technology tend to be more available to &quot;the masses,&quot; whereas most mystical Paradigms tend to be more elitist and exclusive. Which does parallel to some extent with the real-life history of priesthoods and mystical societies. But their outright authoritarianism turns me off even more that the hierarchical tendencies of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, to the extent that Awakening is often associated with REALLY believing that YOU are RIGHT, I kinda suspect that my existential and skeptical tendencies would make it less like that I would be a Mage, and more likely that I would be a Sorcerer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T15:34:54-08:00","id":1421857,"title":"","content":"I could see myself fitting in with Verbena, Celestrial Chorus or Orphan, each with a tendency to scientific ideas.<br /> I don't like administration work, so Technocracy would not be my choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T18:51:10-08:00","id":1421899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1421847#post1421847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to say for sure, but I would likely be a Hollow One or an Orphan who practices Chaos Magick; Everything is Chaos, with some Gods and Monsters. Perhaps a Techgnosi? What I like about Chaos Magick is that it's a mystical Paradigm that nonetheless focuses on tapping into or harnessing powers around or within us in a way that anyone can practice if they are willing to make the time and the effort, and without making any further assumptions about the One Truth of Everything.<br /> <br /> There are some Traditions that I do like; I might fit in decently with the Sahajiya/CoE in particular. But all of the Traditions involve a relatively strong commitment to some kind of fundamental Truth or Teleology that I'm just not willing to buy into 100%. Similarly, one thing I do like about the more idealistic side of the Technocracy/OoR, and idea that getting into MtA really brought to my attention, is the notion that the benefits of science/technology tend to be more available to &amp;quot;the masses,&amp;quot; whereas most mystical Paradigms tend to be more elitist and exclusive. Which does parallel to some extent with the real-life history of priesthoods and mystical societies. But their outright authoritarianism turns me off even more that the hierarchical tendencies of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, to the extent that Awakening is often associated with REALLY believing that YOU are RIGHT, I kinda suspect that my existential and skeptical tendencies would make it less like that I would be a Mage, and more likely that I would be a Sorcerer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But don\u2019t mages have a much more flexible paradigm than sorcerers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T20:21:14-08:00","id":1421926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1421899#post1421899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But don\u2019t mages have a much more flexible paradigm than sorcerers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Comparing the &quot;paradigms&quot; of Mages and Sorcerers in that way is a bit of an apples-to-oranges comparison.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's a reflection of not having read enough Mage source material, but it has often seemed as though becoming one of the Awakened is largely based in the determination, conviction, faith, etc., of the prospective Mage. To make your Will into Reality and overcome the Consensus, you need to REALLY believe that it's possible. To use of an example that's possibly overused but very accessible, in <i>The Matrix</i> when Morpheus is taking Neo through those training simulations, he tells Neo that he can jump the gap between the buildings, and then he even shows Neo that it can be done. And then Neo still fails, because there is believing and then there is BELIEVING. Perhaps I am wrong, but it seems like that capacity for BELIEVING, instead of just believing, is potentially one of the likely conditions for Awakening. And while there are many things that I am passionate about and believe in, there are probably very few things which I BELIEVE in, especially regarding Truth instead of just the perception of Reality.<br /> <br /> Now, to contrast, a Sorcerer does not need to Awaken, they simply need to uncover the secrets of Sorcery. Unlike the Dynamic Magic of Mages, Static Magic works because of some connection to Reality, the Consensus, etc. It is about as much an objective fact of the World of Darkness as gravity. My statement is essentially that, lacking the powerful BELIEF necessary to become a Mage, my interests in the occult and magic could still lead me to uncover the secrets of Sorcery in a more skeptical empiricist fashion.<br /> <br /> That being said, the fact that Paradigms like &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot; are supported, in M20 at least, does lend credence to the idea that fence-sitters who won't commit too much to any one cosmological model may still have their place among the Awakened, so there's always hope <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T04:14:51-08:00","id":1421972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1421926#post1421926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Comparing the &amp;quot;paradigms&amp;quot; of Mages and Sorcerers in that way is a bit of an apples-to-oranges comparison.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's a reflection of not having read enough Mage source material, but it has often seemed as though becoming one of the Awakened is largely based in the determination, conviction, faith, etc., of the prospective Mage. To make your Will into Reality and overcome the Consensus, you need to REALLY believe that it's possible. To use of an example that's possibly overused but very accessible, in <i>The Matrix</i> when Morpheus is taking Neo through those training simulations, he tells Neo that he can jump the gap between the buildings, and then he even shows Neo that it can be done. And then Neo still fails, because there is believing and then there is BELIEVING. Perhaps I am wrong, but it seems like that capacity for BELIEVING, instead of just believing, is potentially one of the likely conditions for Awakening. And while there are many things that I am passionate about and believe in, there are probably very few things which I BELIEVE in, especially regarding Truth instead of just the perception of Reality.<br /> <br /> Now, to contrast, a Sorcerer does not need to Awaken, they simply need to uncover the secrets of Sorcery. Unlike the Dynamic Magic of Mages, Static Magic works because of some connection to Reality, the Consensus, etc. It is about as much an objective fact of the World of Darkness as gravity. My statement is essentially that, lacking the powerful BELIEF necessary to become a Mage, my interests in the occult and magic could still lead me to uncover the secrets of Sorcery in a more skeptical empiricist fashion.<br /> <br /> That being said, the fact that Paradigms like &amp;quot;Everything is Chaos&amp;quot; are supported, in M20 at least, does lend credence to the idea that fence-sitters who won't commit too much to any one cosmological model may still have their place among the Awakened, so there's always hope <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Very good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T09:02:10-08:00","id":1422043,"title":"","content":"Me? Virtual Adepts all the way, with <i>Everything is Data</i> and <i>Reality Hacking</i>. I have leanings toward and sympathy with the Celestial Chorus; but I wouldn't actually <i>be</i> one. Likewise with the Sons of Ether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T01:08:51-08:00","id":1422194,"title":"","content":"Vaelderman, Old Faith or Spirit-talker. If I had to pick a Modern Tradition then either a Dreamspeaker or very weird Verbena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T03:21:24-08:00","id":1422211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1422194#post1422194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vaelderman, Old Faith or Spirit-talker. If I had to pick a Modern Tradition then either a Dreamspeaker or very weird Verbena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome \ud83d\ude0a. I would be Old Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T10:46:53-08:00","id":1422260,"title":"","content":"If we're talking dark ages. Definitely Vaeldermen. I'm already a Norse Polytheist IRL so that's halfway there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T11:01:05-08:00","id":1422264,"title":"","content":"If we're talking Dark Ages, it's a toss-up between Messianic Voices and Craftmasons. But neither is a particularly good fit, because I wasn't raised in the dark ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:43:32-08:00","id":1422345,"title":"","content":"Ideally Sons of Ether or Void Engineer, but who has that kind of energy and motivation, y'know? So more likely Orphan or possibly even Marauder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T06:08:42-08:00","id":1422418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1422345#post1422345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideally Sons of Ether or Void Engineer, but who has that kind of energy and motivation, y'know? So more likely Orphan or possibly even Marauder.</div> </div> </div> </div>so true,<br /> <br /> I'd give a shot at euthanatos or cyberpunk,<br /> but frankly, I'd rather there was some faction for lazy people...maybe hollow ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T11:55:00-08:00","id":1422463,"title":"","content":"Catholic Mysticism is my jam... so, don\u2019t laugh, but the closest actual tradition/craft to that is actually Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> Specifically the magick they work via using meditation and ritual to seek union with god forms... only Catholic Mysticism would mean you only seek spiritual union and to align your will with God instead of different gods depending on what magic you wished to manifest. To be fair though, God being omnipotent means you don\u2019t need union with Zeus for lightning or Hermes for speed.<br /> <br /> The main limitation of that paradigm though is that God only grants gifts for His purposes and to bring about the good. Normal Euthanatos could seek union with a god of time to stop time and allow you to rob a bank unseen for any reason... the Catholic Mystic Euthanatos could probably only use the same effect to, say, save someone from an oncoming truck and robbing a bank would be right out barring something like a stolen object residing in a lockbox that is needed by its true owner.<br /> <br /> My starting spheres would probably be Life 2-3, Mind 2-3 and perhaps Spirit 1-2.<br /> <br /> ETA: and my patron saint would certainly be Saint Michael the Archangel; leader of God\u2019s armies and the Angel of Death (he comes at the hour of death to offer one last chance at salvation thereby consternating the plans of the Devil and lead the righteous to Heaven).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 11-07-2020, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T08:18:47-08:00","id":1422596,"title":"","content":"Order of Hermes: language, meaning, hermeneutics, history, writing, music analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25217-deadcandance13","name":"DeadCanDance13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T13:07:10-08:00","id":1422648,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages Order of Hermes, Akashic Brotherhood, or maybe Orphans. Alot of it depends on my mood or aesthetic I'm going for. Sometimes some mixture (although I do have more affinity for Dark Ages approach to magic than the sphere system as a matter of taste.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T14:51:13-08:00","id":1422667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1422264#post1422264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking Dark Ages, it's a toss-up between Messianic Voices and Craftmasons. But neither is a particularly good fit, because I wasn't raised in the dark ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is of course a difficulty. One thing to believe in a similar faith, another to adapt it to the realities of the past well enough to work magic with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T08:53:07-08:00","id":1422748,"title":"","content":"Hollow One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T19:19:32-08:00","id":1422860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1412912-which-mage-faction-do-you-fit-in-with-and-why?p=1422667#post1422667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is of course a difficulty. One thing to believe in a similar faith, another to adapt it to the realities of the past well enough to work magic with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, my difficulty is that there's no Dark Ages Fellowship with a belief that's in line with \u201cEverything is Data\u201d. At least, no <i>published</i> Fellowship. I believe that there was a Greek group somewhere based on the teachings of Pythagoras, which might be similar enough to my own fascination with mathematics. But my own views would be more something like that with a religious spin, something that the Dark Ages Fellowships aren't really set up to facilitate. And it also likely wouldn't have the libertine spirit of the Virtual Adepts (a major reason why I, as a conservative in real life, appreciate the VAs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T02:29:20-08:00","id":1424671,"title":"","content":"Cult of Ecstasy, push the limits of time, life, and mind, with some basis in chaos magic. Would add that Creation is Innately Divine and Alive would be the paradigm, most likely. This isn't necessarily a perfect match for who I am, but I think it's where I'd end up if Mage-style magick were a thing and I could practice it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-18-2020, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}